      "headline": "External Scaffolding: Why Every Solo Driver Needs a Spotter",
      "keyInsight": "We love the myth of the lone genius pulling themselves up by their boots. Science tells a very different story. Your brain is wired to hide its own blind spots. When you look in the mirror, your mind automatically edits out small errors. You rationalize skipping reps or cutting corners. That is why the best performers never work in a vacuum. A great coach does not grant you magical wisdom. They simply stand where you cannot stand. They hold up an undistorted mirror. Left alone, your brain treats comfort as safety and drifts off course. When you invite formal guidance, you outsource your honesty to someone who cannot be tricked by your excuses. Accountability works best when it lives outside your own skull.",
